{"G1543":{"id":"G1543","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1543","disambiguated_id":"G1543 =","unique_id":"G1543","headword":"ἑκατόνταρχος","transliteration":"hekatontarchos","lexical_morphology":"G:N-M","gloss_en":"centurion","definition_en":"ἑκατοντάρχης (-άρχος, Mat.8:5, 8 27:54, Luk.7:2, Act.22:25 28:16; cf. M, Pr., 48); -ου \n (ἑκατόν, ἄρχω,), [in LXX for מֵאָה שַׂר ;] \na centurion: Mat.8:13, Luk.7:6 23:47, Act.10:1, 22 21:32 22:26 23:17, 23 24:23 27:1, 6 27:11, 31 27:43 (cf. κεντυρίως).†\n (AS)","source_line":1683}],"occurrence_count":20,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"centurião","count":16},{"gloss":"centuriões","count":3},{"gloss":"de-um-centurião","count":1}]},"G1740":{"id":"G1740","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1740","disambiguated_id":"G1740 =","unique_id":"G1740","headword":"ἐνδοξάζομαι","transliteration":"endoxazomai","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"be glorified","definition_en":"ἐν-δοξάζω \n [in LXX for כָּבַד ni., Exo.14:4, 17-18, Eze.28:22, etc.; for עָרַץ, Psa.89:7; Sir.38:6, al. ;] \nto glorify: pass., 2Th.1:10-12.†\n (AS)","source_line":1881}],"occurrence_count":2,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"glorificado","count":2}]},"G2958":{"id":"G2958","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G2958","disambiguated_id":"G2958 =","unique_id":"G2958","headword":"Κυρήνιος","transliteration":"Kurēnios","lexical_morphology":"N:N-M-P","gloss_en":"Quirinius","definition_en":"Κυρήνιος\n (prop. -ίνιος, see Bl., 13; -ῖνος L, -εῖνος, Tr., WH, mg.), -ου, ὁ, \nQuirinus, prop. Quirinius: Luk.2:2.†\n (AS)","source_line":3153}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"Quirino","count":1}]},"G3466":{"id":"G3466","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G3466","disambiguated_id":"G3466 =","unique_id":"G3466","headword":"μυστήριον","transliteration":"mustērion","lexical_morphology":"G:N-N","gloss_en":"mystery","definition_en":"μυστήρισν, -ου, τό\n (μυέω), [in LXX: Dan LXX TH Dan.2:18 ff. (רָז), Tob.12:7, 11, Jdth.2:2, Wis.2:22 6:22 14:15, 23, Sir.3:18 22:22 27:16-17, 21, 2Ma.13:21 * ;] \n__1. that which is known to the μύστης (initiated), a mystery or secret doctrine, mostly in pl., τὰ μ. (Æsch., Hdt., al.). \n __2. In later writers (Menand., Incert., 168), that which may not be revealed (not, however, as in the modern sense, intrinsically difficult to understand), a secret or mystery of any kind (To, Jth, 2Mac, ll, with). \n __3. In NT, of the counsels of God (cf. Th.: Job.15:8, Psa.25:14 for סוֹד), once hidden but now revealed in the Gospel or some fact thereof; \n __(a) of the Christian revelation generally : Rom.16:25, 1Co.2:7, Col.1:26-27, Eph.3:3, 9; τ. βασιλείας τ. θεοῦ, Mrk.4:11; τ. θεοῦ, 1Co.2:1, Rev.10:7; τ. θ., Χριστοῦ, Col.2:2; τ. Χριστοῦ., Col.4:3, Eph.3:4; τ. θελήματος αὐτοῦ, Eph.1:9; τ. εὐαγγελίον, Eph.6:19; τ. πίστεως, 1Ti.3:9; τ. εὐσεβείας, 1Ti.3:16; \n __(b) of particular truths, or details, of the Christian revelation : Rom.11:25, 1Co.15:51, Eph.5:32, 2Th.2:7, Rev.1:20 17:5, 7; pl., τὰ μ., 1Co.13:2 14:2; θεοῦ, 1Co.4:1; τ. βασιλείας τ. οὐρανῶν (θεοῦ), Mat.13:11, Luk.8:10 (cf. Westc., Eph., 180 ff.; AR, Eph., 234 ff.; Lft., Col., 165 f.; Hatch, Essays, 57 f.; DB, iii, 465 ff.; DCG, ii, 213 ff.).†\n (AS)","source_line":3579}],"occurrence_count":26,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"mistério","count":21},{"gloss":"mistérios","count":5}]},"G3604":{"id":"G3604","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G3604","disambiguated_id":"G3604 = the Greek of","unique_id":"H5818G","headword":"Ὀζίας","transliteration":"Ozias","lexical_morphology":"N:N-M-P","gloss_en":"Uzziah","definition_en":"Ὀζείας (Rec. Ὀζίας), -ου, ὁ (Heb. עֻזִּיָּה), \n Uzziah: Mat.18:1-35 9:1-38.†\n (AS)","source_line":3718}],"occurrence_count":2,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"Uzias","count":2}]},"G4134":{"id":"G4134","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G4134","disambiguated_id":"G4134 =","unique_id":"G4134","headword":"πλήρης","transliteration":"plērēs","lexical_morphology":"G:A","gloss_en":"full","definition_en":"πλήρης, -ες \n [in LXX chiefly for מָלֵא ;] \n__1. full, filled: Mat.14:20 15:37; with genitive of thing(s), Mrk.8:19; λέπρας, Luk.5:12; metaphorically, of the soul: πνεύματος ἀγίου, Luk.4:1, Act.6:3 7:55 11:24; πίστεως, Act.6:5; χάριτος, ib. Act.6:8; χ. καὶ ἀληθείας (where π. is indecl.; see M, Pr., 50; Milligan, NTD, 65, with reff. in each), Jhn.1:14; δόλου, Act.13:10; θυμοῦ, Act.19:28; ἔργων ἀγαθῶν, Act.9:36. \n __2. full, complete: μισθός, II Jn 8; σῖτος (π. prob. in­decl. here; see on Jhn.1:14, supr.), Mrk.4:28.†\n (AS)","source_line":4259}],"occurrence_count":16,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"cheio","count":9},{"gloss":"cheios","count":4},{"gloss":"cheia","count":1},{"gloss":"encheram","count":1},{"gloss":"completa","count":1}]},"G4177":{"id":"G4177","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G4177","disambiguated_id":"G4177 =","unique_id":"G4177","headword":"πολίτης","transliteration":"politēs","lexical_morphology":"G:N-M","gloss_en":"citizen","definition_en":"πολίτης, -ου, ὁ\n (πόλις), [in LXX chiefly for רֵעַ ;] \n__1. a citizen: with genitive loc., Luk.15:15, Act.21:39. \n __2. a fellow-citizen: with genitive of person(s), Luk.19:14, Heb.8:11\" (LXX) .†\n (AS)","source_line":4306}],"occurrence_count":4,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"cidadãos","count":3},{"gloss":"conterrâneo","count":1}]},"G4410":{"id":"G4410","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G4410","disambiguated_id":"G4410 =","unique_id":"G4410","headword":"πρωτοκαθεδρία","transliteration":"prōtokathedria","lexical_morphology":"G:N-F","gloss_en":"seat of honor","definition_en":"πρωτοκαθεδρία, -ας, ἡ\n (πρῶιος, καθέδρα), \nthe chief seat: Mat.23:6, Mrk.12:39 (see Swete, in l), Luk.11:43 20:46.†\n (AS)","source_line":4540}],"occurrence_count":4,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"primeiras-cadeiras","count":3},{"gloss":"primeiros-assentos","count":1}]},"G4573":{"id":"G4573","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G4573","disambigua